{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having abdominal pain and vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started about 10 days ago, but got much worse in the last few days. Yesterday was the worst—had one episode of vomiting food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Does the pain get worse with movement?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, moving makes it worse. But eating doesn’t seem to affect it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any fevers, chills, or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fevers or chills. Weight’s been stable. But my colostomy output has decreased, and the stool is like rabbit pellets. One was whitish."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s helpful. I also see you mentioned a neighbor had similar symptoms?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, she had nausea and stomach issues too. Thought maybe it was something going around."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possible, but given your history of lymphoma and bowel surgery, we need to be cautious. We’ve ordered a CT scan to check for any blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could this be related to my lymphoma coming back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible, but we won’t know until we see the scan. The thickening in the bowel could be infection, inflammation, or early lymphoma. We’ll start you on IV fluids and antibiotics just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’m on so many meds already—will they change anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2153-04-16 20:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding metformin while you’re not eating much. Otherwise, we’ll keep your other meds running—like your methadone for pain and Cymbalta for mood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT results are back. There’s a segment of small bowel that’s dilated near a past surgical connection. There’s fecalized material and some new wall thickening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a blockage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It looks like a partial functional obstruction—your bowel isn’t moving things through well. The anastomosis is open, so it’s not a complete blockage. We’re calling GI and colorectal surgery to review."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the thickening—could it be lymphoma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We can’t rule it out, but there’s no clear evidence of progression. Your lymph nodes haven’t changed much, and your spleen is only mildly enlarged, as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2153-04-16 22:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on antibiotics for now—cefepime and flagyl—just in case it’s infection. But if you stay afebrile and improve, we’ll stop them. No surgery needed at this point."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, actually. Pain is much less. Haven’t vomited again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your labs show your white count dropped a bit, but it’s likely due to your immune condition. Stool tests came back negative—no C. diff, no parasites, no salmonella."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it doesn’t look like it. We’re going to stop the antibiotics. GI thinks this was a temporary motility issue—maybe a functional obstruction that’s resolving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the lymphoma concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Still can’t rule it out completely, but no signs of active disease. Your head MRI was done yesterday—results pending, but no red flags so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my colostomy—will it go back to normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2153-04-17 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, output should normalize as your bowel function improves. We’ll advance your diet today—start with clear liquids, then soft foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well on the soft diet—no nausea, pain is gone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No pain, and I’ve had a few good meals. Colostomy is more active now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll keep you overnight for observation. GI wants you to get a magnetic resonance enterography—MRE—after discharge to check bowel function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that like a CT or MRI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s an MRI focused on the bowel. It gives better detail than CT for soft tissue and motility. You’ll need to schedule it within the next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll call radiology. Any other follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2153-04-17 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your regular meds, including IVIG—your next dose is due soon. And keep your oncology follow-up. Call if you develop fever, severe pain, or stop passing stool."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. Your exam is normal, labs are stable, and you’ve tolerated regular food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. So the obstruction is gone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it appears resolved. We don’t think it was cancer-related. But the MRE will help confirm everything’s moving properly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was really worried it was the lymphoma back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But right now, everything points to a temporary issue. Keep up with your specialists, and we’ll stay on top of any changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2153-04-18 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if anything comes up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2153-04-16 19:38:00",
    "admission_end": "2153-04-18 15:13:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with a history of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) of the colon and CNS, status post bowel resection and colostomy, was admitted for worsening abdominal pain, nausea, and vomiting over 10 days, with recent deterioration. Imaging revealed a dilated segment of small bowel near a jejunojejunal anastomosis with fecalized material and new wall thickening, suggestive of a functional small bowel obstruction. Infectious causes were ruled out by negative stool studies. She improved clinically with supportive care and antibiotics, which were discontinued due to lack of infection signs. Surgical intervention was not required. The obstruction resolved, and she tolerated a diet advance. She was discharged home with plans for outpatient magnetic resonance enterography to evaluate bowel function, while continuing management of chronic conditions including DLBCL in remission, common variable immunodeficiency, diabetes, and chronic pain.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Common variable immunodeficiency",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Colostomy status",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Lumbago",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
